Fillets: the piece patch 1310 adds past the spine's end lies on the end
piece's own surface, one face with it (mitcad#1349).

Where an analytic blend's contact reaches the face at the end only past the
spine's end vertex, that face going on tangentially, ChFi3d_KPartCutToEnd
runs the end edge's blend on past the end and adds the piece cut there
(patch 1310). ChFi3d_KPartCutPiece makes each piece's surface a copy of the
blend's, so the piece past the end became a face of its own beside the end
piece P (a torus face of 0.07 mm2 at each side of a fin's end), where the
stored body has one torus face. The piece past the end now takes P's surface
where that surface is the blend's own (the same points at the piece's
contact), so the two are one face.

Test: geometry/tests/test_fillet_fin_top_creases.cpp,
test_transitions_cut_by_their_pieces (with 1350 and 1351): the rounding has
the stored body's faces.

Upstream: new.

